# Composition patterns

- Do not add boolean props to switch modes or UI states (`isLoading`, `isEmpty`, `isEditing`). Prefer composition.
- Prefer compound components that share context over prop-drilling configuration.
- Lift shared state into a provider so sibling parts can access it.
- The provider is the only place that knows how state is implemented. Expose a context shaped as `{ state, actions, meta }`.
- Prefer explicit variant components for lifecycle UI (`FeatureLoading`, `FeatureError`, `FeatureEmpty`, `FeatureSuccess`) instead of one component with conditional flags.
- Prefer `children` for composition over `renderX` props.

```tsx
// Prefer
<FeatureProvider>
  <Feature.Toolbar />
  <FeatureLoading />
  <FeatureError />
  <FeatureEmpty />
  <Feature.Table />
</FeatureProvider>

// Avoid
<Feature isLoading isEmpty hasError showToolbar />
```
